    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0564" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg484"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 856.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter from Senator
                    Mark A. Hanna, setting forth the circumstances under which Charles H. Toe Water
                    was taken prisoner of war by the British forces.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to ask that the matter be investigated, and to report the
                    result.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that Mr. Water’s release from detention is asked for on
                    parole. Should the circumstances turn out to be as stated in Senator Hanna’s
                    letter, however, you will at once, without awaiting further instructions,
                    request that he be released unconditionally.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d482-a1.xml" xpointer="d482-a1"/>
            </div>
